  "description": "The proposed work is for 3 Lime trees to have the crown pruned and reduced overall by 1 meter - 1m crown reduction in width and 2m reduction in height, leaving a canopy spread of 10m and height of 12m\r\nAll three trees are situated together to the right hand side of the main gate to 216 Gort Lodge in Sudbrook Lane.",
  "site_name": "Gort Lodge",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The specification is not suitable and therefore needs to be confirmed. The specification needs to be measurable and quantifiable so that we can understand the amount that is to be removed in meters. We need to know the amount to be removed and the remaining crown size. E.g. 2m crown reduction in width and 2m reduction in height, leaving a canopy spread of 3m and height of 5m"
